    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "USE OF PROCEEDS We estimate that the net proceeds from our issuance and sale of shares of our common stock (or pre-funded warrants in lieu thereof) in this offering will be approximately $19.6\u00a0million after deducting the underwriting discounts and commissions and estimated offering expenses payable by us, assuming full exercise of the pre-funded warrants but no exercise of the warrants offered hereby. We currently intend to use the net proceeds from this offering, if any, for the continued clinical development of our lead compound buntanetap in clinical studies for Alzheimer\u2019s disease and Parkinson\u2019s Disease, and for working capital and general corporate purposes. The amounts and timing of our use of the net proceeds from this offering will depend on a number of factors, such as the timing and progress of any partnering efforts, any strategic transactions in which we may engage, and the ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk Factors You should read the \u201cRisk Factors\u201d section of this prospectus supplement, as well as those risk factors that are incorporated by reference in this prospectus supplement and the accompanying prospectus, for a discussion of factors to consider carefully before deciding to purchase our securities. Purchase by Company Insiders One of our directors is participating in this offering. Such director has agreed to purchase an aggregate of 5,000,000 shares of common stock and accompanying warrants, for an aggregate purchase price of approximately $5,000,000. The purchase price per share and accompanying warrants for such Company insider is the same as being paid by other investors in this offering. NYSE symbol \u201cANVS\u201d The number of shares of our common stock to be outstanding immediately after this offering is based on 43,022,520 shares of common stock outstanding as of November 3, 202",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
